s you can figure out a way to  either get people to upgrade to a new  one  or find a completely new market of  people  who are willing to buy one and i'm here  to tell you  that apple has figured it out but before  i tell you how  let's get into the second major issue  for apple  and that's feature saturation when apple  released their series 5 watch last year  they immediately discontinued the series  4.  they did that because it was almost the  same exact watch  in fact there were only three changes  the always-on display 32 gigs of storage  instead of 16 and the compass feature  that's it and even last month they  revealed the series 6  while immediately discontinuing the  series 5  for the exact same reason this time  there are only  6 changes the red and blue finishes  the always on altimeter the blood oxygen  sensor  the brighter always on display while in  direct sunlight  the faster processor and the ultra  wideband chip  now while there are more changes than  before a lot of those things don't  really matter to someone who already has  the series 5  and that's why my brother max is  returning the apple watch series 6.  that's also why i'm not buying it for my  wife  she already has the series 4 and she  says she's completely happy with it and  it does everything she wants it to do  that's called feature saturation when  your apple watch  is so feature-rich already that it's  very hard to think of groundbreaking new  features  that'll make people want to upgrade to  the latest model so from apple's point  of view  this is a problem especially if they  want to continue selling apple watches  for the next 5 to 10 years which their  investors  are counting on so i'm here to tell you  that apple has figured it out  and it all starts with the name the  apple watch sc  back in april of this year apple  released the brand new iphone se  and they had three main goals for that  iphone at least in my opinion  goal number one was to make it  affordable for other countries like  china and  india where the bulk of the smartphone  market share  goes to lower priced phones and at 399  dollars for an iphone  with the latest chip it's definitely a  great value  goal number two was to get people who  were still using older iphones  like the iphone 5 the iphone 6 and the  iphone 7  to upgrade 400 bucks for a brand new  iphone with the latest chip  a brand new battery and a familiar  design  is definitely enough to get non-techie  users to upgrade  and it even attracted a bunch of android  users as well  which brings us into goal number three  make an affordable smartphone that's a  great choice for parents  to buy for their kids mainly young  teenagers  399 dollars is very reasonable for an  iphone  but here's the secret that most people  don't think about  if you're a teen and the first phone you  own is an iphone  you're much more likely to upgrade to  another iphone in the future  since you've now become comfortable with  the operating system  and there you go apple has another  lifetime apple customer  that's much more likely to buy apple  devices and pay  for apple services and that finally  brings us to  the apple watch se it's basically got  almost all the same features as the  series 6  but it's only 279 dollars  so this is what can finally get those  people  who still own an older apple watch to  upgrade  but that's not even the biggest deal out  of  all of the new features apple released  this year for the apple watch  the absolute most important feature is  the new family setup feature now you can  set up an apple watch for someone who  doesn't have an iphone  this means someone with an android phone  can now use an apple watch  an elderly person with health issues can  now use an apple watch without an  iphone and most importantly a child  can now have an apple watch without an  iphone  now if you think that's crazy it  actually makes a whole lot of sense  compared to buying a smartphone for your  child compared to even the cheapest  iphone  the iphone sc for 399 you can get the  apple watch sc  with lte for 329  which is the model you want for family  setup on top of that  cellular service for wearables is  significantly cheaper  than getting another smartphone line for  example  t-mobile charges 28 dollars per line  for the absolute cheapest plan and  that's if you have a total of four lines  but to add a wearables device it's  literally only  ten dollars a month per device so you're  saving money  on every front by going with an apple  watch  instead of an iphone so for a child  ranging from ages 8  to around 13 or maybe even 15 an  apple watch makes sense because you  don't have to worry about them dropping  and cracking their iphone  or even worse losing it it's always on  their wrist so you can track their  location at any time  you can text them or call them no matter  where they are  and you don't have to worry about them  browsing the web on sites they shouldn't  be looking at  or maybe even worse using tick tock you  can manage who they're able to  communicate with  and you can even send cash directly to  their apple watch  which they can spend at any place that  supports apple pay  it's basically the perfect solution for  keeping in touch with children that  aren't  old enough or responsible enough to have  their own smartphone  and i personally think that buying apple  watches for kids  is gonna become a trend within one to  two years  if you think about it when everything  goes back to normal and kids start going  back to class  every single kid in the classroom will  notice the apple watch  on that one kid's wrist and that kid is  gonna show off his new memoji watch face  that looks exactly like him and just  like what happened with the airpods  every single kid in the classroom is  gonna want  an apple watch and there is one thing i  know for sure  that child apple watch user is almost  guaranteed to become an apple watch user  in the future  which means they're also likely to  become an iphone user as well  so to wrap all of this up if you're in  apple's shoes  and the apple watch has just about  reached peak levels of market saturation  and feature saturation what do you do  you spark a new trend of apple watches  for kids  and you secure the future generation of  users who will eventually be much more  likely  to buy apple products and services when  they grow up  and that is apple's master plan  for the apple watch sc and here's a  little bit of proof that apple is quite  literally planning this  why do you think they release the solo  loot bands that you simply stretch onto  your wrist  because it's meant to be easier for kids  as well as the elderly oh and by the way  i forgot to share my experience with the  apple watch sc  it's basically been great and if you  don't care about the always on display  or the added health features just buy  the se  especially if you want to get an lte  model since you'll save 170 bucks  compared to the series 6. and there you  guys have it  hopefully you enjoyed my marketing focus  review of the apple watch se  and if you did go ahead and click the  circle to subscribe for more videos like  this one  and consider checking out our apple  product merch like this t-shirt  right over there and watch that video  whatever it is  up there thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next one

